{"paper": "SSC-DelhiPoliceHC-10-Oct-2022-Shift2.pdf", "status": "ok", "mode": "sequential", "splitter": "qdot", "section_slice": true, "extracted_count": 20, "tagged_count": 20, "questions": [{"n": 1, "text": "X, Y and Z can do a piece of work in 10 days, 20 days and 30 days, respectively. In how many days can the work be completed if X is assisted by Y and Z together, on every alternate day?", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "alternate-days", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 2, "text": "", "options": [], "options_source": "missing", "image_only": true, "topic": "Number System", "sub": "fractions-decimals", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 3, "text": "What is the HCF of 11, 44, 121, 88 and 1331?", "options": [{"text": "22", "added": false}, {"text": "11", "added": false}, {"text": "8", "added": false}, {"text": "2", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "HCF-LCM", "sub": "hcf-lcm-of-numbers", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 4, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "83", "added": false}, {"text": "48", "added": false}, {"text": "74", "added": false}, {"text": "35", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Data Interpretation", "sub": "bar-graph", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 5, "text": "If 6 men or 8 women can do a work in 86 days, then how many days will 14 men and 10 women take to complete the same work?", "options": [{"text": "30", "added": false}, {"text": "28", "added": false}, {"text": "24", "added": false}, {"text": "25", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Work", "sub": "group-work", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 6, "text": "The cost of 3 shirts and 2 pants is ₹950, while the cost of 2 shirts and 3 pants is ₹1,050. What is the cost of 4 pants and 5 shirts?", "options": [{"text": "₹1,685", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,780", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,750", "added": false}, {"text": "₹1,850", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "linear-equations", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 7, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "38 : 47", "added": false}, {"text": "36 : 43", "added": false}, {"text": "45 : 32", "added": false}, {"text": "46 : 39", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Algebra", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 8, "text": "A digital note-pad is available for ₹25,000 cash or ₹2,500 down payment followed by 4 equal monthly instalments. If the rate of interest charged is 24% per annum simple interest, what is the monthly instalment (in ₹, rounded off to the nearest tens)?", "options": [{"text": "5,890", "added": false}, {"text": "5,800", "added": false}, {"text": "5,900", "added": false}, {"text": "5,790", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Simple Interest", "sub": "si-instalments", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 9, "text": "In a proportion, the 1st , 2nd and 4th terms are 15, 25 and 75, respectively. What is the 3rd term?", "options": [{"text": "35", "added": false}, {"text": "65", "added": false}, {"text": "55", "added": false}, {"text": "45", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Ratio-Proportion", "sub": "proportion", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 10, "text": "What is the average of the first five positive multiples of 5?", "options": [{"text": "15", "added": false}, {"text": "16", "added": false}, {"text": "75", "added": false}, {"text": "80", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Average", "sub": "series-average", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 11, "text": "A car takes 5 hours to cover a distance if it travels at a speed of 40 km/h. What should be its speed to cover the same distance in 2.5 hours?", "options": [{"text": "40 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "60 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "80 km/h", "added": false}, {"text": "20 km/h", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Time-Speed-Distance", "sub": "basic-tsd", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 12, "text": "A wall 12 m long, 9 m high and 90 cm thick is to be constructed. Given that one pack contains 450 bricks, how many packs of bricks will be required if each brick is of dimensions 10 cm x 7.5 cm x 7 cm and the cement and sand mixture occupies one- eighteenth volume of the wall? (Rounded off to the nearest integer)", "options": [{"text": "390", "added": false}, {"text": "389", "added": false}, {"text": "388", "added": false}, {"text": "387", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Mensuration 3D", "sub": "cube-cuboid", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 13, "text": "If in ΔABC and ΔPQR, AB = 8 cm, BC = 10 cm, AC = 12 cm, PQ = 8 cm, QR = 10 cm and PR = 12 cm, then which of the following is true?", "options": [{"text": "ΔABC ≅ ΔQPR", "added": false}, {"text": "ΔABC ≅ ΔQRP", "added": false}, {"text": "ΔABC ≅ ΔRPQ", "added": false}, {"text": "ΔABC ≅ ΔPQR", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Geometry", "sub": "congruence-and-similarity", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 14, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "cos⁡6 θ⋅cot⁡5 θ", "added": false}, {"text": "-cot⁡6 θ⋅cot⁡5 θ", "added": false}, {"text": "cot⁡6 θ⋅cos⁡5 θ", "added": false}, {"text": "cos⁡6 θ⋅cos⁡5 θ", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Trigonometry", "sub": "identities", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 15, "text": "Nikita would gain 20% by selling a table fan for Rs.840 and would gain 12% by selling a wall clock for Rs.1,008. She sells the table fan for Rs.980, what is the least price for which she must sell the wall clock to avoid any loss on the two together?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.660", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.640", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.600", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.620", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Profit-Loss", "sub": "successive-transactions", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 16, "text": "The price of fruits is increased by 25%. How much per cent should the consumption be decreased so that expenditure remains the same?", "options": [{"text": "10%", "added": false}, {"text": "15%", "added": false}, {"text": "25%", "added": false}, {"text": "20%", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Percentage", "sub": "increase-decrease", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 17, "text": "", "options": [{"text": "155", "added": false}, {"text": "150", "added": false}, {"text": "160", "added": false}, {"text": "165", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": true, "topic": "Simplification", "sub": "bodmas", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 18, "text": "A shopkeeper offers a 40% discount on items. He offers a further discount of 10% on the reduced price for the first 100 customers. What does a customer under 100 has to pay for an item of Rs.1,000?", "options": [{"text": "Rs.780", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.650", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.430", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.540", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Discount", "sub": "successive-discounts", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 19, "text": "A person borrowed a sum of Rs.8,000 at the rate of 10% p.a. compounded semi-annually. The compound interest for a period of one year is:", "options": [{"text": "Rs.820", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.800", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,600", "added": false}, {"text": "Rs.1,680", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false, "topic": "Compound Interest", "sub": "compounding-frequency", "key_answer": null}, {"n": 20, "text": "Calculate the volume of a cylinder whose base area is 40 cm2 and the height is 9 cm.", "options": [{"text": "120 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "300 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "180 cm3", "added": false}, {"text": "360 cm3", "added": false}], "options_source": "real", "image_only": false